As Jukka S Lahtinen puts it in rec.games.hack:
> Mjholtz@saturn.otago.ac.nz (Michael) writes:

> >you feel sick  deathly sick

> Sounds like you keep eating too old corpses. If you find something that died
> in a trap (or otherwise find already dead without seeing it die), DON'T
> eat it, it's rotten. I don't know exactly how fast corpses get tainted,
> but generally you should eat them within a few moves or forget it.
> (Except lizards, they don't get tainted. There may be other exceptions,
> but I don't know for sure.) And I THINK the rotting speed is different with
> different monsters.

However, there are some other option available to you...
- If you have a unicorn horn, you can cure the sickness.
- If you have waited the prayer timeout, there is a monster that you
	REALLY need an intrisic from  (ie floating eye), then you
	can eat it and then pray afterwards.
- Monsters that die on ice do not rot.
- NEVER ever never never ever never eat corpses of the undead beings. ;)

